tasks.details:
Basis: a published LeanKit risk-register practice (Andrew Doran, 2021) — “the card itself will keep a history of its journey in its audit log”. Flowline has the log (`ItemLogEntry`: created / blocked / unblocked / archived / unarchived / noted / limit) and the Activity tab that renders it, but movements are exactly what it does not record, so a card's past is unrecoverable. Task 59 (flow metrics: cycle time, lead time, throughput, cumulative flow) names movement history as its precondition; task 15 (comments and activity) would want it too.

Add `moved` to `ItemLogKind` and append `logEntry('moved', …)` wherever a placement's lane changes:
- `moveCard` (store.ts) — already returns early when the target lane is the current one, so a rank-only reorder is *not* a move and must stay that way;
- `moveInitiative` — same rule; note it refuses a cross-section move, so a recorded move never crosses a section;
- the index paths (`moveCardToIndex` / `moveInitiativeToIndex` → `placeCard`), which are how drag-and-drop lands a card at a position;
- the **implicit** rehoming inside `splitLane` and `removeLane` — there a card changes cell because the board was edited, not because a person moved it. Record these too (the card genuinely moved) with a note saying why (“lane split” / “lane removed”), because silent cell changes are exactly the thing a history should explain.

What the entry carries — SETTLE THIS and record the answer: the cleanest is optional `fromLaneId` / `toLaneId` on the entry for linkage, plus the `note` holding the names as they were at that moment (“Dev → Test”). History is what was true then: a lane renamed or deleted later must not rewrite it, and the panel must render an entry whose lane no longer exists without a lookup failing.

Non-goals: no new derived field on `Item` (status stays derived from the cell), no change to `Placement.laneEnteredAt` — it stays the age source for `laneAges` / staleness (task 69) and is stamped on the same events; the log is the whole journey, the placement is where it is now. `ItemLogKind` grows by one member and all new fields are optional, so old persisted state reads unchanged: **no persist version bump, no migrate**, and export/import already carries `Item.log` (WORKSPACE_KEYS unchanged).

Surface: the item panel's Activity tab — `ItemPanel.tsx` maps a dot colour per kind (line ~56), so `moved` needs its own; entries read “Moved: Dev → Test” and carry a timestamp like every other event. This is what task 59 then reads, so 59 needs no new recording machinery.
